
Web Conference
--------------

This collection of scripts creates a conferencing system for the web,
by creating an interface to Usenet news, or simulating a news system
if none exists.

Contents:

archive.sh    - An archive script I use
conference.pl - Creates a confernece index
mail2conf.pl  - Pipes mail to a numbered list of messages in a directory.
                Use this if you do not have a news system.
mail2news.sh  - Pipes e-mail into a newsgroup (not original with me)
message.pl    - PERL script to display a conference message.

Set-Up
------

This system requires a standard Unix setup (sendmail and INN), but you can
do without the INN if you need to. The main thing is how you set up your
sendmail aliases file to gateway mail into a news spool, or a newspool
equivalent. I also have majordomo running on all my conferences so
that some can get it via e-mail.

For a confernece that is based on news running here is an example of what
I have in my aliases files for a newsgroup called austin-jesus:

#
#  austin-jesus
#
owner-austin-jesus: admin@example.com
austin-jesus: "| /usr/local/majordomo/wrapper resend -l austin-jesus -h cfi.org
-r austin-jesus austin-jesus-outgoing"
austin-jesus-approval: owner-austin-jesus
austin-jesus-outgoing: :include:/usr/local/majordomo/lists/austin-jesus,usenet-a
ustin-jesus,austin-jesus-archive, "| /usr/local/majordomo/wrapper digest -r -C -
l austin-jesus-digest austin-jesus-digest-outgoing"
owner-austin-jesus-outgoing: owner-austin-jesus
austin-jesus-request: "| /usr/local/majordomo/wrapper majordomo -l austin-jesus"
owner-austin-jesus-request: owner-austin-jesus
austin-jesus-archive: "| /usr/local/majordomo/wrapper archive \
 -f /d1/ftp/pub/ccn/austin-jesus -m -a"
owner-austin-jesus-archive: owner-austin-jesus
usenet-austin-jesus: "| /usr/local/mail2news/mail2news -n austin.jesus"
 
The key is the usenet-austin-jesus line the gateways the mail into Usenet
news.

For a machine without INN running, or a conference not based on a Usenet
type newsgroup I do this for a group called Padres:

#
#  padres
#
owner-padres:
padres: "| /usr/local/majordomo/wrapper resend -l padres -h cfi.org -r padres pa
dres-outgoing"
padres-approval: owner-padres
padres-outgoing: :include:/usr/local/majordomo/lists/padres,padres-archive,padre
s-conf
owner-padres-outgoing: owner-padres
padres-request: "| /usr/local/majordomo/wrapper majordomo -l padres"
owner-padres-request: owner-padres
padres-archive: "| /usr/local/majordomo/wrapper archive \
 -f /d1/ftp/pub/ccn/padres -m -a"
owner-padres-archive: owner-padres
padres-conf: "| /d3/httpd/cfi_local/forums/mail2conf.pl padres"

The key is the last line. You will need to change the path to what
you have.

Once you have the gateways set up to access a newsgroup you will need to
do some editing of the perl scripts to your paths, and to taste.

To actually use the conference, say for example the Padres newsgroup just
type:

  http://www.cfi.org/cgi-bin/confernece.pl?padres

Unless it is a secret group, you may want to include this as a link somewhere.

See my home page for a examples of these groups in action.

